Package: PRIMErepair
Type: Package
Title: Budgeted Certification of Minimum-Cost Prediction Alternatives
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Hongdong", "Hao", email = "h294866@foxmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Selects minimum-input-cost prediction alternatives from a locked
    candidate library subject to finite-pool, groupwise binary Brier-loss
    constraints. Provides deterministic support certificates, separate
    without-replacement confidence-sequence modes, shared-label portfolio
    replay, and fixed-budget LURE point-estimation comparators. Candidate
    predictions and public group definitions are fixed before querying labels.
    Implements task adaptations of Waudby-Smith and Ramdas (2020)
    <https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper/2020/hash/e96c7de8f6390b1e6c71556e4e0a4959-Abstract.html>,
    Hara et al. (2024) <doi:10.1007/s10994-024-06603-1>, and
    Kossen et al. (2021) <https://proceedings.mlr.press/v139/kossen21a.html>.
    Certificates concern the specified finite pool, not future populations.
    Does not train models, identify leakage sources, or establish clinical safety.
